# Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in. The server and the sell command load it on start.
# Check what live mode still needs, without printing any values:
#   uv run python -m yardsale.bureau_server --check

# Claude, for the Identifier and Appraiser. Create one in the Anthropic Console.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Apify, for the Researcher's eBay sold-listings search (about $0.08 per photo).
# Apify Console > Settings > API & Integrations.
APIFY_TOKEN=

# ASI:One's model (asi1-mini) reads what people type in the ASI:One chat, such as a seller's own
# price or what a buyer is looking for. Without it, a simpler keyword reader is used, and sellers
# still approve every price before anything is listed. https://asi1.ai/developer
ASI_ONE_API_KEY=

# The campus product: same-school only. Every new ASI:One conversation starts with "Are you a
# student?" and a school email, buyers only see their own school's listings, and trades get a
# meeting spot on campus. Off unless set. With it on, a chat without a school email can neither
# list nor search, and the question only goes out on a conversation's first message.
# YARDSALE_CAMPUS=1

# Optional. Puts real coordinates and a Google Maps link on the campus meeting places Yardsale
# names (Places API text search, billed per request). Without it a place keeps its name and the
# chat simply sends no map link. Google Cloud console > APIs & Services > Credentials.
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# Optional. Connects the Market, Identifier, Researcher, and Appraiser to your Agentverse account
# at startup. Without it, the server logs an Inspector link for each one to connect by hand.
AGENTVERSE_API_KEY=

# Optional, live mode. Host up to this many item agents on Agentverse (needs AGENTVERSE_API_KEY);
# the rest run in this server. Agentverse limits how many agents an account has (reportedly 8
# free, 25 on Premium), and the Market, Identifier, Researcher, Appraiser, Market Scout, Deal
# Finder, and buyer agent already use 7, so 18 fills a 25-agent account.
# The server deletes a hosted agent once its item is sold or taken down.
#   uv run python -m yardsale.hosting --list      # see them; --cleanup deletes sold ones
# YARDSALE_HOST_ITEMS=18
# Give hosted item agents a picture of the item, drawn by ASI:One and kept in a public Apify
# key-value store (needs ASI_ONE_API_KEY and APIFY_TOKEN). Off unless set.
# YARDSALE_ITEM_AVATARS=1

# Payment links for closed deals. Test mode only: live keys and Visa's production host are
# refused. Set Visa's keys, Stripe's, or both (Visa is used first; YARDSALE_PAYMENTS picks one).
# Visa Pay By Link, from the Visa Acceptance sandbox Business Center (Payment Configuration >
# Key Management > REST shared secret key):
# VISA_MERCHANT_ID=
# VISA_KEY_ID=
# VISA_SHARED_SECRET=
# VISA_API_BASE=https://apitest.visaacceptance.com
# Stripe Checkout, with a test key from the Stripe dashboard (Developers > API keys):
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
# YARDSALE_PAYMENTS=visa            # visa, stripe, or none
# YARDSALE_COMMISSION_PERCENT=5     # Yardsale's cut of each sale; the seller gets the rest
# YARDSALE_PAYMENT_RETURN_URL=https://asi1.ai

# Optional. Every order status change is POSTed here as JSON, signed with the secret
# (X-Yardsale-Signature: sha256=<hex HMAC of the body>). Buyers' identities are never sent.
# YARDSALE_ORDERS_WEBHOOK=https://example.com/yardsale-orders
# YARDSALE_ORDERS_SECRET=

# Optional. An HTTP API for @yardsale, the Fetch Business agent (its OpenAPI integration, a
# "Business Tool"), on 127.0.0.1:YARDSALE_API_PORT. The key is what Fetch Business sends in the
# X-Yardsale-Key header; make one with: python3 -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))"
# Make it public with: cloudflared tunnel --no-autoupdate --protocol http2 --url http://127.0.0.1:8110
# The description (/openapi.json) names the URL it was fetched through; YARDSALE_API_URL overrides it.
# YARDSALE_API_KEY=
# YARDSALE_API_PORT=8110
# YARDSALE_API_URL=https://your-tunnel.trycloudflare.com

# Optional. Lets sellers also list on their own eBay account: they connect it on eBay's consent
# page (OAuth), and Yardsale answers eBay Best Offers with its haggling rules. One developer
# keyset from developer.ebay.com (Application Keys). Under User Tokens, make a RuName and set its
# auth accepted URL (and declined URL) to <YARDSALE_API_URL or tunnel>/ebay/callback; this needs
# YARDSALE_API_KEY, since the callback is on that HTTP API. Sandbox unless YARDSALE_EBAY_ENV is
# production. Not yet tried against eBay.
# EBAY_CLIENT_ID=
# EBAY_CLIENT_SECRET=
# EBAY_RUNAME=
# YARDSALE_EBAY_ENV=sandbox
# Optional. Craigslist by email: the seller posts by hand ("craigslist 1" in the chat gives the
# text) with this inbox as the posting's email, and each item's agent haggles with buyers who
# email it. The server reads this inbox every 10 seconds and replies through Craigslist's relay.
# Use a Gmail account made for this, with 2-Step Verification on and an app password
# (myaccount.google.com/apppasswords), never the account's own password. Check the login with:
#   uv run python -m yardsale.craigslist_mail --check
# YARDSALE_MAIL_ADDRESS=yardsale.demo@gmail.com
# YARDSALE_MAIL_PASSWORD=
# YARDSALE_IMAP_HOST=imap.gmail.com
# YARDSALE_SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
# Set to 0 if Craigslist's relay strips links: buyers are asked for a phone number instead, and
# the seller sees the payment link under "my listings" to text it.
# YARDSALE_MAIL_LINKS=1

# Live mode only. The public URL that forwards to this machine's Bureau port (8100), such as an
# ngrok or cloud URL. Item agents advertise it on the Almanac; /submit is added if missing.
# Without it they advertise 127.0.0.1, which only this machine can reach.
# YARDSALE_PUBLIC_URL=https://your-tunnel.example.app

# Optional overrides.
# YARDSALE_ASI_MODEL=asi1-mini
# YARDSALE_CLAUDE_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5
# YARDSALE_CLAUDE_EFFORT=medium
# YARDSALE_APIFY_ACTOR=caffein.dev~ebay-sold-listings
# Other sites a buyer's search falls back to (APIFY_TOKEN; each search is a paid run per site).
# The Market Scout searches the same sites for live asking prices when a photo is priced.
# YARDSALE_CRAIGSLIST_CITY=sfbay
# YARDSALE_OFFERUP_ZIP=94103
# Where sellers are, for the Scout's local searches (OfferUp): a 5-digit ZIP code.
# YARDSALE_ZIP=94103
# Facebook Marketplace is the dearest, so it's off unless this is 1.
# YARDSALE_FACEBOOK=1
# YARDSALE_FACEBOOK_CITY=sanfrancisco
# YARDSALE_BUREAU_PORT=8100
# YARDSALE_BUYER_PORT=8101
# YARDSALE_SELLER_PORT=8102
# Listings database. Default: .agent-data/yardsale-bureau/listings-<live|offline>.sqlite3
# YARDSALE_DB=
# Every agent address comes from the master seed. By default it's generated once into
# .agent-data/yardsale-bureau/master_seed. Set this only to move a deployment to a new machine
# with the same addresses, and keep it secret: it controls every Yardsale agent.
# YARDSALE_MASTER_SEED=
